<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Vindhyashakti</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">3rd century</span> · <a href="/centuries/3rd-century">3rd century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Vindhyashakti was the founder of the Vakataka dynasty, which rose in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/deccan">Deccan</a> of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/india">India</a> in the mid-3rd century as the Satavahana dynasty broke up. He is known from a Vakataka inscription at Ajanta and from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/puranas">Puranas</a>, which name him as a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brahmins">Brahmin</a> chief. His son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/pravarasena-i">Pravarasena I</a> turned the family's domain into a large kingdom across central India.</p></div>
